# Synthetic constellation lines for the RenderableInterpolatedConstellationLines
# example. Timestep 0 (initial keyframe).
#
# Each `mesh -c <colorIndex> { ... }` block declares one constellation. The values are
# in parsecs; the asset selects this with `Unit = "pc"`. The set of `id`s and the number
# of vertices for each id must match across all three timestep files.

mesh -c 1 {
id TRI
3
10.0 0.0 0.0
15.0 10.0 5.0
20.0 0.0 0.0
}

mesh -c 1 {
id QUA
4
-25.0 5.0 0.0
-15.0 5.0 0.0
-15.0 -5.0 0.0
-25.0 -5.0 0.0
}

mesh -c 2 {
id LIN
2
0.0 10.0 0.0
0.0 20.0 0.0
}
